{"name":"Green Flash","hex":"#79c753","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green flash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rare phenomenon observed in the morning or evening when the sun is crossing or immediately below the horizon, in which a momentary flash or ray of green light appears above the upper rim of the solar disk, caused by the refraction of light in the atmosphere."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green_flash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Green flash","blocks":[{"text":"The green flash and green ray are meteorological optical phenomena that sometimes occur transiently around the moment of sunset or sunrise. When the conditions are right, a distinct green spot is briefly visible above the Sun's upper limb; the green appearance usually lasts for no more than two seconds. Rarely, the green flash can resemble a green ray shooting up from the sunset or sunrise point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Development_of_Green_Flash.jpg/330px-Development_of_Green_Flash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_flash","wikidata":"Q647349"},{"title":"Green Flash (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Green Flash\" is the 39th single by the Japanese idol girl group AKB48, released in Japan on March 4, 2015. This single was first revealed during the group's Request Hour 2015 concert."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/26/Green_Flash_Limited_A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Flash_(song)","wikidata":"Q18998046"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Big_green_flash.JPG/500px-Big_green_flash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Big_green_flash.JPG/1280px-Big_green_flash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Big_green_flash.JPG/500px-Big_green_flash.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A green flash in Santa Cruz, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABig_green_flash.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg/500px-Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg/1280px-Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg/500px-Inferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The stages of a green flash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInferior_Mirage_green_flash.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/GreenFlash.jpg/500px-GreenFlash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/GreenFlash.jpg/1280px-GreenFlash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/GreenFlash.jpg/500px-GreenFlash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A mock-mirage green flash observed in San Francisco, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreenFlash.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Green_rim_of_the_setting_sun.jpg/500px-Green_rim_of_the_setting_sun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Green_rim_of_the_setting_sun.jpg/500px-Green_rim_of_the_setting_sun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The upper rim is green while the lower one is red, as the sun sets behind the Golden Gate Bridge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreen_rim_of_the_setting_sun.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Green_rim_and_green_flashes_in_SF.jpg/500px-Green_rim_and_green_flashes_in_SF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Green_rim_and_green_flashes_in_SF.jpg/1280px-Green_rim_and_green_flashes_in_SF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut